WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.549
Eight out of ten buildings in Europe
were constructed before 1990.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.240
These buildings are structurally weaker,
consume lots of energy

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.739
and are at greater risk of seismic losses
as requirements were lower some decades ago.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.671
National authorities find it hard to develop plans
to renovate buildings on such a scale.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.511
The task requires a huge amount
of information and technical knowledge.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.400
Could we help them choose the best
strengthening technologies&nbsp;

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.706
for their specific types of buildings?

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.497
Could we support them also by involving
engineers, architects and construction companies?

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.880
We provide technical guidelines to help
them do this large-scale planning,&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.243
all backed by data and impact 
evaluation tools they can directly use.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.480
We started by producing a set
of technical guidelines.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.320
We chose regions in Europe
where renovating would make the biggest impact,&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.963
whether because their buildings were older
or because the seismic risk was high,&nbsp;and often both.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.760
We then created a web platform
to attract the interest of national authorities&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.966
and disseminate these guidelines.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.880
As information is key,&nbsp;

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.640
we share evaluations of the efficiency
of different technologies,&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.600
their cost and a measure of their impact
during the entire life cycle.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.857
We have even developed a methodology to assess 
the multiple cumulative benefits&nbsp;of strengthening buildings

00:01:35.203 --> 00:01:41.936
This can be used to estimate the economic gains 
of lowering energy bills&nbsp;and of reducing seismic losses.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.500
We analyzed 105 million buildings 
in the European Union.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:53.609
We identified the top 20 priority regions
where almost 12 million people live.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.000
Our recommendations can now
directly feed into renovation plans&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.160
that could benefit millions of Europeans.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.520
We are a team of European Commission
scientists and experts from across Europe&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.618
who work together on the integrated seismic
and energy renovation of buildings

